---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const p='/equipment/13-06/';
const br='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MSD/brochures/glacios-2-cryo-tem-br0158.pdf';
const ds='https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MSD/Datasheets/glacios2-cryo-tem-smart-epu-falcon4i-direct-electron-ds0491.pdf';
const inst='https://www.zmb.uzh.ch/en/Available-Systems/ElectronMicroscopes/TEMTFSGLACIOS2.html';
const refs=[
 ['front-quarter.webp','Closed right-front quarter: ivory cabinet, dark vertical fascia, blue band and side service seams.',br+'#page=1','Thermo Fisher BR0158, p. 1'],
 ['front-elevation.webp','Front elevation: front fascia width, inactive display and lower division. The flat display deliberately omits operating UI.',ds+'#page=2','Thermo Fisher DS0491, p. 2']
];
const checks=[
 ['Native center A / row-major index','1,132 and (30, 50) nm','1,132 and (30, 50) nm','exact'],
 ['A–B distance in both views','60 nm','60 nm','exact'],
 ['Native / reflected orientation determinant','+384 / −384 px²','+384 / −384 px²','exact'],
 ['Default / narrow linear window for A','228 / 255 ADU','228 / 255 ADU','exact, raw unchanged'],
 ['Malformed mirror or reversed contrast','Rejected','Rejected','expected error'],
 ['Metric reference block geometry','1.25 × 0.93 × 2.14 m','1.25 × 0.93 × 2.14 m','1 μm against authored dimensions only']
];
---
<Layout documentTitle="Glacios 2 · Dormant cabinet and synthetic image archive" description="Explore the Glacios 2 enclosure and compare two archived geometric rasters. No hardware operation or microscopy acquisition.">
 <main id="gla2">
  <p class="navline"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-06/">← Equipment record 13-06</a></p>
  <p class="series">LABORATORY EQUIPMENT / 13-06 / DOCUMENTARY EXHIBIT</p>
  <h1>Glacios 2 Cryo-TEM</h1>
  <p class="lead">Inspect the dormant instrument, then switch between a synthetic geometric raster and its saved mirror. Try narrowing the display window. The image contrast changes, but the stored pixels, sample identifier and scale stay the same.</p>
  <div class="duo">
   <section class="card">
    <h2>Metric 3D enclosure</h2>
    <div id="ga-view" class="viewer"></div><p id="ga-model" role="status">Loading cabinet and detached exhibit…</p>
    <div class="actions" aria-label="3D viewpoints">
     <button type="button" data-ga-view="orbit">Reset orbit</button><button type="button" data-ga-view="front">Front</button><button type="button" data-ga-view="side">Right flank</button><button type="button" data-ga-view="archive">Detached exhibit</button>
    </div>
    <p>Orbit by dragging, zoom by scroll or pinch. Tap the detached image panel to cycle the fixed archive; no cabinet surface is interactive.</p>
   </section>
   <section class="card">
    <h2>Read-only inert archive</h2>
    <canvas id="ga-raster" width="448" height="448" aria-label="Preauthored inert geometric image; choose coordinates below for keyboard use."></canvas>
    <div class="inputs">
     <label>Stored image<select id="ga-image"><option value="0">A · Native</option><option value="1">M · Mirror X</option></select></label>
     <label>Dark limit (ADU)<input id="ga-low" type="number" min="0" max="254" step="1" value="0"/></label>
     <label>Bright limit (ADU)<input id="ga-high" type="number" min="1" max="255" step="1" value="255"/></label>
     <label>Column<input id="ga-x" type="number" min="0" max="55" step="1" value="12"/></label>
     <label>Row<input id="ga-y" type="number" min="0" max="55" step="1" value="20"/></label>
    </div>
    <div class="actions"><button id="ga-next" type="button" disabled>Next stored image</button><button id="ga-reset" type="button">Reset review</button><button id="ga-export" type="button" disabled>Export review JSON</button></div>
    <p id="ga-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading synthetic archive…</p>
    <p id="ga-summary" class="readout"></p><p id="ga-pixel" class="readout"></p>
   </section>
  </div>
  <section>
   <h2>Configuration and illustrated references</h2>
   <p>This is the Thermo Scientific <strong>Glacios 2</strong> cabinet, not the older Glacios or current Glacios 3. The exterior follows the publicly depicted chassis. The detector, internal column, loading equipment, support racks, and manufacturer workstation are not represented; the detachable review stand is an original exhibit, not an accessory or workstation.</p>
   <div class="refs">
    {refs.map(([f,label,href,source])=><figure><img src={p+f} alt={label} width="780" height="590" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Original reference-based rendering.</strong> {label} <a href={href}>{source} (original image)</a>.</figcaption></figure>)}
   </div>
   <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Value</th><th>Evidence / role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
     <tr><td>Cabinet model envelope, H × W × D</td><td>≈ 2.20 × 1.28 × 0.99 m including exterior relief</td><td>Authorial scale estimate, not measured or vendor-approved; appearance from <a href={br+'#page=1'}>BR0158 p. 1</a> and <a href={ds+'#page=2'}>DS0491 p. 2</a>. Rear panel generic.</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Generation / instrument class</td><td>Glacios 2 cryogenic transmission electron microscope</td><td><a href={inst}>University of Zurich instrument identity</a>; documentary only.</td></tr>
     <tr><td>Synthetic archive frame</td><td>56 × 56 px, 2.5 nm/px</td><td><a href={p+'fixture.json'}>Original inert fixture</a>. Invented coordinate label, not a detector or specimen scale.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
   </table></div>
  </section>
  <section>
   <h2>How the read-only review works</h2>
   <p>The fixed archive contains two unsigned 8-bit images of an asymmetric inert symbol. The pixel index is <code>row × 56 + column</code>. Using the upper-left pixel center as the origin, X increases right and Y increases down; each step is 2.5 synthetic nm. Mirror X maps a column <code>x</code> to <code>55 − x</code>. Handedness in this explicitly 2D coordinate convention is represented by the sign of the landmark determinant, not by physical 3D chirality or reconstruction.</p>
   <p>The grayscale display is <code>round(255 × clamp((raw − dark)/(bright − dark), 0, 1))</code>. It never edits archive values. Invalid indices, coordinates and display limits are rejected and leave the prior view untouched. The export includes the sample ID, revision, raw value, display range and both archive and source image IDs.</p>
   <p><strong>Limits:</strong> no image acquisition, cryogenic or specimen workflow, imaging/beam settings, hardware control or reconstruction. The viewer is a metric browser/VR-authoring asset with a named target; immersive headset operation has not been verified.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
   <h2>Verification</h2>
   <p>Known synthetic case: A = (12,20), B = (36,20), C = (18,36). Independently, 24 px × 2.5 nm/px gives 60 nm, and the 24-by-16-pixel signed area product is 384 px². Reflection reverses that sign without changing the distance. These checks are not an experimental comparison or manufacturer calibration.</p>
   <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(([name,x,y,t])=><tr><td>{name}</td><td>{x}</td><td>{y}</td><td>{t}</td><td>Pass</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
   <p><a href={p+'verification.json'}>Machine-readable results</a> · <a href={p+'contract.json'}>Input/output contract</a> · <a href={p+'example-review.json'}>Example review</a> · <a href={p+'fixture.json'}>Synthetic archive</a> · <a href={p+'build-fixture.py'}>Fixture source</a></p>
   <p><a href={p+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender model source</a> · <a href={p+'glacios2.glb'} download>Download metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'interaction.json'}>Interaction manifest</a> · <a href={p+'asset-metrics.json'}>GLB metrics</a></p>
  </section>
 </main>
</Layout>
<script>
import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-06/client.mjs';
</script>
<style>
main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:1.2rem clamp(.9rem,2.5vw,2rem) 3rem}
.series,.readout,table,input,select,button{font-family:var(--font-label,system-ui,sans-serif)}
.series{font-size:.78rem;letter-spacing:.13em}.lead{max-width:72ch}
.duo,.refs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.2rem 0}
.card{border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 30%,transparent);padding:1rem;border-radius:.25rem}
.viewer{height:clamp(23rem,45vw,32rem);overflow:hidden;background:#263949}
.viewer :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%;touch-action:none}
#ga-raster{display:block;width:min(100%,26rem);height:auto;background:#263949;margin:.5rem auto 1rem}
.actions,.inputs{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.6rem 0}
button,input,select{background:transparent;color:inherit;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 50%,transparent);border-radius:.2rem;padding:.5rem;font-size:.91rem;min-height:2.6rem}
button{cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}input{width:5.5rem}label{display:grid;font-size:.86rem;gap:.25rem}
figure{margin:0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figcaption{font-size:.92rem;margin:.45rem 0}
section{margin:1.5rem 0}.duo section{margin:0}
.tablewrap{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.88rem}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 25%,transparent);text-align:left;padding:.5rem;vertical-align:top}
[data-error=true]{font-weight:bold;color:var(--accent,currentColor)}
@media(max-width:770px){.duo,.refs{grid-template-columns:1fr}.viewer{height:22rem}}
</style>
